<hr data-start=3D"362" data-end=3D"365">
<h2 data-start=3D"367" data-end=3D"394"><strong data-start=3D"370" data-end=
=3D"394">Step 2: What happens</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"396" data-end=3D"417"><strong data-start=3D"400" data-end=
=3D"417">Before fork()</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"418" data-end=3D"507">
<li data-start=3D"418" data-end=3D"457">
<p data-start=3D"420" data-end=3D"457">We start with <strong data-start=3D"=
434" data-end=3D"449">one process</strong> (<code data-start=3D"451" data-e=
nd=3D"455">P0</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"458" data-end=3D"507">
<p data-start=3D"460" data-end=3D"507">It prints <code data-start=3D"470" d=
ata-end=3D"481">"Hello\n"</code> <strong data-start=3D"482" data-end=3D"490=
">once</strong> before <code data-start=3D"498" data-end=3D"506">fork()</co=
de>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"509" data-end=3D"512">
<h3 data-start=3D"514" data-end=3D"531"><strong data-start=3D"518" data-end=
=3D"531">At fork()</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"532" data-end=3D"583">
<li data-start=3D"532" data-end=3D"583">
<p data-start=3D"534" data-end=3D"583"><code data-start=3D"534" data-end=3D=
"538">P0</code> calls <code data-start=3D"545" data-end=3D"553">fork()</cod=
e>, creating a new process <code data-start=3D"578" data-end=3D"582">P1</co=
de>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"585" data-end=3D"617">Now we have <strong data-start=3D"59=
7" data-end=3D"614">two processes</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"618" data-end=3D"650">
<li data-start=3D"618" data-end=3D"635">
<p data-start=3D"620" data-end=3D"635">Parent (<code data-start=3D"628" dat=
a-end=3D"632">P0</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"636" data-end=3D"650">
<p data-start=3D"638" data-end=3D"650">Child (<code data-start=3D"645" data=
-end=3D"649">P1</code>)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"652" data-end=3D"744">Both <strong data-start=3D"657" data=
-end=3D"669">continue</strong> execution <strong data-start=3D"680" data-en=
d=3D"689">after</strong> <code data-start=3D"690" data-end=3D"698">fork()</=
code> =E2=80=94 i.e., both run the <code data-start=3D"720" data-end=3D"725=
">for</code> loop from <code data-start=3D"736" data-end=3D"743">i =3D 0</c=
ode>.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"746" data-end=3D"749">
<h3 data-start=3D"751" data-end=3D"782"><strong data-start=3D"755" data-end=
=3D"782">Important: Variable <code data-start=3D"777" data-end=3D"780">i</c=
ode></strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"783" data-end=3D"989">
<li data-start=3D"783" data-end=3D"843">
<p data-start=3D"785" data-end=3D"843"><code data-start=3D"785" data-end=3D=
"788">i</code> is <strong data-start=3D"792" data-end=3D"802">global</stron=
g> and initialized to 0 at program start.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"844" data-end=3D"907">
<p data-start=3D"846" data-end=3D"907">At <code data-start=3D"849" data-end=
=3D"857">fork()</code>, <strong data-start=3D"859" data-end=3D"897">both pr=
ocesses have their own copy</strong> of <code data-start=3D"901" data-end=
=3D"904">i</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"908" data-end=3D"989">
<p data-start=3D"910" data-end=3D"989"><code data-start=3D"910" data-end=3D=
"914">P0</code> and <code data-start=3D"919" data-end=3D"923">P1</code> wil=
l each run the loop <strong data-start=3D"947" data-end=3D"964">independent=
ly</strong> from <code data-start=3D"970" data-end=3D"977">i =3D 0</code> t=
o <code data-start=3D"981" data-end=3D"988">i =3D 3</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"991" data-end=3D"994">
<h3 data-start=3D"996" data-end=3D"1018"><strong data-start=3D"1000" data-e=
nd=3D"1018">Loop Execution</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1019" data-end=3D"1039">
<li data-start=3D"1019" data-end=3D"1039">
<p data-start=3D"1021" data-end=3D"1039">Each process runs:</p>
</li>
</ul>
